  "body": "## Goal\nTrack historical gate failures by changed file and boost likely or recent failures in the impact ranker.\n\n## Scope\n- Define an append-only rolling JSONL file (`failures.jsonl`, capped at 500 runs) that records commit SHA, UTC time, changed file paths, failed test names, and step durations.\n- Add a pure ranker module in `xtask` that scores each test by empirical co-failure probability given changed files divided by duration from `timings.tsv`.\n- Add a decaying boost for recent failures and a boost for new tests that have no history entry.\n- Follow file renames using `git diff -M` so moved files keep prior co-failure history.\n- Skip corrupt lines with a diagnostic note instead of failing the gate.\n- Connect the history score to `cargo xtask impact` and `cargo xtask gate batch --failure-history`.\n\n## Done means\n`xtask` reads and appends `failures.jsonl`, ranks tests by co-failure rate divided by duration with recency and new-test boosts, handles renamed files and corrupt lines safely, and passes unit tests.\n\nPart of #2738",
